implementationPlan.description:
Add one case per branch of the per-kind wipe rule. Edit only packages/moe-daemon/src/state/massDeletionHeal.test.ts, and only with the main session's Edit tool (project rail: no shell writes and no subagent edits to tracked files). Make exactly two edits; the existing 8 cases, both beforeEach fixtures and the helpers stay byte-unchanged.
(a) Line 8 becomes: import { healMassDeletion, MASS_DELETION_FRACTION, MASS_DELETION_MIN } from './massDeletionHeal.js';  Both constants are exported at massDeletionHeal.ts:38 and :40.
(b) Append the two cases below inside the second describe ('healMassDeletion on a board-tracking project (runtime dirs wiped, board kept)'), after its last case ('never applies the per-kind rule to the board kinds a git checkout changes on purpose', which ends at line 206) and before the describe's closing line 207, with one blank line before each case. They reuse that describe's beforeEach unchanged (4 workers, 1 team, 3 proposals, 1 resource 'box-heal', 1 attempt; the before counts [4, 1, 3, 1, 1] are pinned at :141) and its in-scope names (before, entriesOf, fileOf, RUNTIME_DIRS, workerIds, taskIds, moePath, state). Keep the titles' '(z1) ' and '(z2) ' prefixes exactly: checkRef [1] greps the vitest FAIL lines for them.

  it('(z1) rewrites runtime kinds whose directories are gone though each held fewer than MASS_DELETION_MIN entries', async () => {
    // Only the dirGone clause can fire: each kind is under MASS_DELETION_MIN, and neither is a combined kind.
    const gone = ['resources', 'attempts'] as const;
    for (const dir of gone) {
      expect(before[dir].length).toBeLessThan(MASS_DELETION_MIN);
      fs.rmSync(path.join(moePath, dir), { recursive: true, force: true });
    }

    expect(await healMassDeletion(state)).toBe(2);
    for (const dir of gone) {
      for (const [id, entity] of before[dir]) {
        expect(JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(fileOf(dir, id), 'utf-8'))).toEqual(entity);
      }
    }

    await state.load();
    for (const dir of RUNTIME_DIRS) expect(entriesOf(dir)).toEqual(before[dir]);
    expect(state.resources.get('box-heal')?.holders.map((h) => h.taskId)).toEqual([taskIds[0]]);
  });

  it('(z2) rewrites a runtime kind that lost MASS_DELETION_MIN and MASS_DELETION_FRACTION of its files, directory kept', async () => {
    // Only the per-kind fraction branch can fire: 3 of 4 workers, dir kept; 3 of 59 combined is 5%.
    const lost = workerIds.slice(0, 3);
    const combinedKnown = state.tasks.size + state.epics.size + state.teams.size + state.workers.size + state.proposals.size;
    expect(lost.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(MASS_DELETION_MIN);
    expect(lost.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(workerIds.length * MASS_DELETION_FRACTION);
    expect(lost.length).toBeLessThan(combinedKnown * MASS_DELETION_FRACTION);
    for (const id of lost) fs.rmSync(fileOf('workers', id));

    expect(await healMassDeletion(state)).toBe(3);
    const was = new Map(before.workers);
    for (const id of lost) expect(JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(fileOf('workers', id), 'utf-8'))).toEqual(was.get(id));

    await state.load();
    for (const dir of RUNTIME_DIRS) expect(entriesOf(dir)).toEqual(before[dir]);
  });

Why each shape isolates one branch of massDeletionHeal.ts:94 (`!BOARD_KINDS.has(dir) && (dirGone || isWipe(lost, entries.size))`):
- (z1) resources and attempts each hold 1 entry, so isWipe(1, 1) is false (1 < MASS_DELETION_MIN), and neither is in COMBINED_KINDS (:60), so the combined rule sees 0 losses. Only dirGone can wipe them, and the heal must return 2.
- (z2) the workers directory stays, so dirGone is false, and 3 of the 59 combined entities (50 tasks + 1 epic + 1 team + 4 workers + 3 proposals) is 5%, under the 20% combined threshold. Only isWipe(3, 4) can wipe workers, and the heal must return 3.
The premise expects make those preconditions fail loudly if the fixture or the constants change. Architect probe at 9657a30c: shipped 10/10; mutant A fails only (z1) with 'expected +0 to be 2'; mutant B fails only (z2) with 'expected +0 to be 3'.
error handling: this is a test-only change, so no production failure path changes; the new test cases use only the describe's mkdtemp dir (its afterEach rmSync cleans it), never the live .moe, and no timers. mem:gotcha-mass-deletion-heal-board-tracking has the fixture recipe and QA's original probe.
